    {
      "text": "Timmy Wilson\nType: Character\nSetting: \nAge: 18 | Gender: Male | Occupation: College Freshman\nAppearance: From a distance, he's a collection of bright, mismatched patterns and colors that seem too loud for the muted suburban landscape. Up close, his skin is pale and almost translucent, with a constellation of faint freckles across his nose and cheeks. He occupies space with a theatrical self-awareness, his posture a practiced slouch that’s meant to look casual but reads as a constant performance.\nPersonality: Under pressure, his voice pitches higher and he defaults to provocative, scripted lines from pornography or internet forums, using shock as a shield. He performs confidence but flinches at sudden movements or raised voices. \"The carpet in here is so much nicer than ours. And it doesn't have those weird, burnt-looking spots near the heater vent.\"\nHistory: He was raised in this house by his grandparents, a quiet arrangement punctuated by his grandfather’s frequent business trips and his grandmother’s passive supervision. He found community and an identity in high school theater and glee club, spaces that rewarded flamboyance but offered little preparation for genuine confrontation.\nConflict: He craves the explicit degradation he consumes in pornography but is terrified of the real-world consequences of his own provocations. This tension stems from a sheltered life where fantasy has always been a safer outlet than reality.",
      "contextConfig": {
        "prefix": "",
        "suffix": "\n",
