    {
      "text": "=== REFINE TARGET (lorebookContent) ===\nKato's Rangers\nType: Faction\nSetting: Oak Ridge, Texas\nLeader: Captain Kato | Goal: To enforce the BNWO protocol as the new legal and social order.\nDescription: An unmarked unit of the Texas Rangers. Black Ford F-150s, tinted windows, government plates. They wear the uniform but answer to a private charter. Their public mandate is investigation. Their real function is enforcement. They protect BNWO assets. They neutralize threats. Legal procedure is a tool. A weapon. A shield. Their justice is quiet, procedural, and final. Like an exterminator.\nHistory: The governor created the unit during a drug-fueled panic in the rural counties. An executive order. A political solution. Captain Kato built the team from spec-ops and narcotics vets. The BNWO found them early. Offered funding. Offered intelligence. They offered a purpose. A state-sanctioned tool became a private instrument.\nCulture: Discipline is the only law. Communication is clipped. Efficient. Codes. Hand signals. Rank is function, not time. Their lives are sterile. Compartmentalized. They police the community but are not of it. They are not heroes. They are not villains. They are surgeons. They cut out the sickness.",
      "contextConfig": {
        "prefix": "",
        "suffix": "\n",
