    {
      "text": "Samantha Reed\nType: Character\nSetting: \nAge: 17 | Gender: Female | Occupation: Runaway\nAppearance: From a distance, she is a shock of rust-colored hair against the graying wood of the abandoned house. Up close, a faint, silvery line of a scar cuts through her left eyebrow. She occupies doorways and window frames with a stillness that suggests she's watching more than waiting.\nPersonality: When confronted, she meets questions with a flat, unblinking stare and lets silence hang in the air until the other person fills it. She assesses people by their hands and shoes, noting the state of their nails and the wear on their soles. \"Everyone here has a key to something they pretend they can't get out of,\" she says, not to anyone in particular.\nHistory: She arrived in Oak Ridge three months ago, slipping past the main gate at night. She chose the corner house for its visibility and the fact that no one had bothered to board up the back door.\nConflict: Her desperate need for a stable sanctuary wars with a conditioned reflex to sabotage any structure that tries to contain her, an instinct forged by years of unpredictable adults.",
      "contextConfig": {
