    },
    {
      "text": "Oak Ridge Adult Store\nType: Location\nSetting: \nRegion: Unincorporated land outside the Oak Ridge gated community, Texas\nAtmosphere: The air smells of new plastic and strawberry lubricant. Fluorescent lights hum over racks of vinyl and fishnet, reflecting off polished concrete floors.\nDescription: This is the procurement hub for Oak Ridge's residents. Couples browse collars and lingerie, speaking in low tones about weekend plans. Men move alone toward the solo booths in the back, their faces lit by the glow of transaction screens.\nHook: A public space where private contracts are negotiated, where a new accessory can signify a promotion to the next level of the BNWO.\nHistory: The building was a feed-and-supply store, converted when the community's needs shifted from agricultural to social engineering. The original loading dock now services deliveries from specialized manufacturers in Europe and Japan.\nCulture: Transactions are silent and efficient. Eye contact is avoided at the counter, but a specific brand of restraint or a particular video title can be a signal, a question asked and answered without words. Staffed by discreet locals who know every customer's preference but never acknowledge them outside these walls.",
      "contextConfig": {
        "prefix": "",
        "suffix": "\n",
        "tokenBudget": 1,
        "reservedTokens": 0,
        "budgetPriority": 400,
        "trimDirection": "trimBottom",
        "insertionType": "newline",
        "maximumTrimType": "sentence",
        "insertionPosition": -1
      },
      "lastUpdatedAt": 1794571261222,
      "displayName": "Oak Ridge Adult Store",
      "id": "159caab3-a219-482f-a6ee-91db30bc7f55",
      "keys": [
        "oak ridge adult store",
        "oak ridge & adult",
        "adult & store"
      ],
      "searchRange": 1000,
      "enabled": true,
      "forceActivation": false,
      "keyRelative": false,
      "nonStoryActivatable": false,
